            <ArticleTitle>Successful treatment of trifurcation and quadrifurcation lesions using a minimal protrusion balloon crush technique.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>21-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8183.2007.00299.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Percutaneous treatment of coronary bifurcation lesions remains a challenging aspect of interventional cardiology, but the approach to trifurcation and quadrifurcation lesions can be considered &quot;double jeopardy.&quot; We describe two cases of trifurcation and one case of quadrifurcation that were treated percutaneously using a &quot;minimal protrusion balloon crush technique.&quot; Immediate and long-term results were favorable with this approach.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
